<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sitka</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as New Archangel, Novo-Arkhangelsk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sitka is a city on Baranof Island in south-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a>. Founded as New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arkhangelsk">Archangel</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-baranov">Alexander Baranov</a> in 1804, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlingit">Tlingit</a> had destroyed an earlier Russian fort in 1802, it became the capital of Russian America in 1808. The transfer of Alaska to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> took place there in 1867, and it remained the territorial capital until 1906.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sitka.jpg" alt="Sitka" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gillfoto · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sitka_84_Elev_135.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
